    <string name="how_title">How CAPJI Net talks to your router</string>
    <string name="how_body">Your phone only controls what the router itself exposes (REST API / ubus / web session). Android can discover devices on the LAN, but it cannot block or throttle other devices on its own - the router must enforce the rules.</string>
    <string name="err_wrong_credentials">Wrong username or password</string>
    <string name="mock_note1">Demo router: every number is simulated (usage runs ~10x faster so quotas fill quickly).</string>
    <string name="mock_note2">On real routers without native quota support, caps are counted by CAPJI Net and only enforced while the app/service runs.</string>
    <string name="mock_note3">Devices with private (randomized) MACs can reappear as new devices and escape MAC-based rules.</string>
    <string name="mt_note1">Live per-device speed is read from the device\'s queue; devices without a queue show 0.</string>
    <string name="mt_note2">Quota and timed pause need a RouterOS script/scheduler and are not available in this driver yet.</string>
    <string name="mt_note3">Rules are keyed by IP: a changed DHCP lease or a randomized MAC can bypass them.</string>
